1
00:05:02,727 --> 00:05:08,727
It is the greatest mystery of all because no human being will ever solve it.

2
00:10:05,454 --> 00:10:11,454
The Omen is a horror, thriller film directed by Richard Donner.

3
00:15:08,181 --> 00:15:14,181
Immediately after their miscarriage, the US diplomat Robert Thorn adopts
the newborn Damien without the knowledge of his wife.

4
00:20:10,909 --> 00:20:16,909
Yet what he doesn’t know is that their new son is the son of the devil.

5
00:25:13,636 --> 00:25:19,636
Robert Thorn, played by Gregory Peck.

6
00:30:16,363 --> 00:30:22,363
Katherine Thorn, played by Lee Remick.

7
00:35:19,090 --> 00:35:25,090
Keith Jennings, played by David Warner.

8
00:40:21,818 --> 00:40:27,818
Mrs. Baylock, played by Billie Whitelaw.

9
00:45:24,545 --> 00:45:30,545
Damien Thorn, played by Harvey Stephens.

10
00:50:27,272 --> 00:50:33,272
Father Brennan, played by Patrick Troughton.

11
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
The Omen is a 1976 supernatural horror film directed by
Richard Donner and written by David Seltzer.

12
01:00:32,727 --> 01:00:38,727
An international co-production of the United Kingdom and the United States, it stars Gregory Peck, Lee Remick, David Warner,
Harvey Spencer Stephens (in his film debut), Billie Whitelaw, Patrick Troughton, Martin Benson, and Leo McKern.

13
01:05:35,454 --> 01:05:41,454
The film's plot follows Damien Thorn, a young child replaced at birth by his father,
unbeknownst to his wife, after their biological child dies shortly after birth.

14
01:10:38,181 --> 01:10:44,181
As a series of mysterious events and violent deaths occur around the family and Damien
enters childhood, they come to learn he is in fact the prophesied Antichrist.

15
01:15:40,909 --> 01:15:46,909
Released theatrically by 20th Century-Fox in June 1976, The Omen received mixed reviews from
critics but was a commercial success, grossing over $60 million at the U.S.

16
01:20:43,636 --> 01:20:49,636
box office and becoming one of the highest-grossing films of 1976.

17
01:25:46,363 --> 01:25:52,363
Retrospective reviews of the film have been more favorable, and the film earned two
Oscar nominations, including a win for Jerry Goldsmith's musical score.

18
01:30:49,090 --> 01:30:55,090
The film spawned the Omen franchise, with Damien – Omen II released two years later, followed by The Final
Conflict (1981) and Omen IV: The Awakening (1991), as well as a 2006 remake and 2024 prequel.

19
01:35:51,818 --> 01:35:57,818
It also spawned a 2016 television series that ran for one season on A&E.

20
01:40:54,545 --> 01:41:00,545
The film explores themes of ambassador, prophecy, monk, photography, nanny.

21
01:45:57,272 --> 01:46:03,272
The tone is dark and intense.
